        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plainwell%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town originated in the 1830s after native peoples were removed from the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plainwell%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A stagecoach line once ran from Kalamazoo to Grand Rapids through Plainwell, later replaced by the Grand Rapids and Indiana Railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plainwell%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Historic Sanborn Fire Insurance Maps of Plainwell, dating back to 1884, show the town’s early downtown layout and businesses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://hometownhistorymaps.com/pages/history-of-plainwell-michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Plainwell hosts an annual Farmers’ Market and a Chocolate Stroll concert series in its downtown park.",
